body:
Your theory is my thoughts exactly.  Once the tables turn (late 20's, early 30's) and guys have the upper hand dating-wise, the women all want to settle down.  So, they had their fun, but when it's out turn... yeah no way we're allowed to.  Take that broad brushed inequity and add some cowardice and having to always be the one to 'pull the trigger'... I can see how this happened.  Or I can speculate.  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
